{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1288662-lunar-creation-animal-or-concept-first","id":1288662,"title":"Lunar creation: Animal or concept first?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-16T11:44:27-08:00","id":1288662,"title":"Lunar creation: Animal or concept first?","content":"I'm just curious, when you create a Lunar, which do you do first? Do you choose an animal totem and create a concept around it? Or do you think of the character concept first then choose an animal totem that fits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T11:56:41-08:00","id":1288664,"title":"","content":"Mostly the animal, but it might be the other way round.<br /> <br /> Sometimes the two come in together. Currently I'm playing a snake-totem snake-stylist. That's not really the case of one or the other coming first.<br /> <br /> Before that, I had an owl-totem shaman, but he was a mortal PC who exalted in-game. So obviously the totem came second.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T12:44:52-08:00","id":1288691,"title":"","content":"When I make characters I generally just have a pile of themes that I pile up, smash together, edit down, and eventually shape into a character. Never having played a lunar before most of the totems I come up with mostly make an as aesthetic statement that highlights said themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T13:50:39-08:00","id":1288722,"title":"","content":"I start with the animal and then start incorporating more elements to the concept. Lunars are prone to having that small hint of &quot;irony&quot; (or lack of) behind them IMO. Like a clever character will tend to have some witty animal for totem.<br /> <br /> I think that's a neat &quot;clich\u00e9&quot;. But if you're more in the One-Piece-type-of-character mood, you can always give an elephant totem to a stealthy character and take the challenge. Lunars are so mutable that it wouldn't be hard to make a character like that, and maybe someone would like to roleplay her as an almost comedic character (which doesn't mean useless).<br /> <br /> Similarly, I start with MA style for sidereal concepts. But that's just me. I'm sure there are plenty of ways to do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T14:01:48-08:00","id":1290097,"title":"","content":"When I'm creating NPCs, the animal usually comes first and can serve as a bit of inspiration to flush out the character concept. When I'm making a character to play, I usually get a conceptual inspiration and then go back and forth over a few choices before finally picking an animal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24219-goddessgood","name":"goddessgood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24219_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T15:31:45-08:00","id":1290121,"title":"","content":"Depends on what I'm going for. Sometimes I have an interesting character and pick an animal that fits. Others I feel like using a particular animal in mind and design an appropriate character to fit. As a general character design note, I tend to identify what I can build effectively using the games mechanics before I put much effort into character creation. I don't think I can get away with a Lunar with a flu virus spirit shape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T15:48:02-08:00","id":1290124,"title":"","content":"It depends.<br /> <br /> Sometimes I have a clear character concept and then find an animal totem that fits it - either straight or somewhat subverted in terms of theme.<br /> <br /> Sometimes I think a particular animal is cool and try to figure out what kind of human would have that kind of animal as a spirit shape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}